                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "éthérées"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b6214965-fa38-4cae-8ad7-7ba1ef762a71",
                        "entry_id": "f335b3af-ec2f-310a-a16a-fb0da884d353",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "éthéréen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9fdbb73d-b94e-3a11-b3b4-dd3a5d1fb5df",
                        "entry_id": "f335b3af-ec2f-310a-a16a-fb0da884d353",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a rapport à l’éther, aux espaces célestes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "poetic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8f12a12-8283-4c7c-98ba-720ee16b9770",
                                "sense_id": "9fdbb73d-b94e-3a11-b3b4-dd3a5d1fb5df",
                                "text": "Astre du jour, brille d’une clarté nouvelle ! ajoute par ton éclat à cette auguste solennité ; dissipe les nuages où se forme la foudre ; que le ciel soit pur, afin que nos chants puissent monter plus librement vers la voûte éthérée !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03e3e389-6dac-4ccd-8b96-4647df3b8766",
                                "sense_id": "9fdbb73d-b94e-3a11-b3b4-dd3a5d1fb5df",
                                "text": "Ami lecteur, félicitez-moi d’avoir un sylphe aussi commode, qui tout aussi bien que celui du prince des philosophes, de Socrate enfin, me transporte avec autant de facilité, tantôt dans les Champs-Elysées, tantôt dans les régions éthérées..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e34dcfd-d655-4653-abd9-a4b674057380",
                                "sense_id": "9fdbb73d-b94e-3a11-b3b4-dd3a5d1fb5df",
                                "text": "N’est-ce pas un voyage aussi que celui de l'esprit, parcourant à la suite de la science les régions lointaines des espaces éthérés, et allant d’étape en étape, c'est-à-dire de soleil en soleil, jusqu’aux derniers confins de l’univers visible ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                        "entry_id": "f335b3af-ec2f-310a-a16a-fb0da884d353",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est ou paraît diaphane, impalpable, immatériel, sublime."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fa7eb7d-21bb-4746-a719-924023053939",
                                "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                                "text": "Il voguait dans les sphères d’un bonheur éthéré, nullement dangereux, lourd de reconnaissance et ne pensant plus à rien, à rien."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5cb00947-3f43-45f7-a8a8-a0e69c175c5c",
                                "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                                "text": "C’est la partie éthérée de ton âme que je veux, c’est ton aspiration brûlante vers le ciel que je veux étreindre et saisir, afin d’être ton ciel et ton âme, comme tu es mon Dieu et ma vie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "27e5bbf2-6fed-4fc7-8e4e-7202946ed602",
                                "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                                "text": "Amour immatériel, pur, éthéré, subtil comme l’haleine du printemps, solide comme l’airain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a61d84bd-0df9-48bc-be80-336d706f6e76",
                                "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                                "text": "Cet homme est si peu élégiaque, si peu éthéré, qu’il ferait horreur même à un notaire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de3303c4-d667-4294-95d5-3556890dbfbb",
                                "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                                "text": "Il jaillit de plus hauts soleils un éclair qui produit lumière et harmonise, son et couleur, lumière spirituelle qui n’a pas de nom ici-bas, mélodie éthérée que les mortels ne peuvent comprendre ni par symboles, ni par énigmes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98cc5ff3-3293-40e7-8ab7-53ea06b90acd",
                                "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                                "text": "Sans doute, cet idéal semble chimérique à plusieurs d’entre vous, mais je suis sûr aussi qu’il paraît désirable à la plupart et que vous apercevez au loin l’image éthérée d’une société pacifique où les hommes désormais réconciliés laisseront rouiller leurs épées, refondront leurs canons et désarmeront leurs vaisseaux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e118110-64bc-45ca-8295-e69480865042",
                                "sense_id": "3e8a7a05-5196-3ebe-81c8-dfd6cfb4566f",
                                "text": "Tout à l’heure, elle deviendra la jeune fille éthérée qu’Augustin Meaulnes aperçoit au cours de la fête étrange, et qu’Alain Fournier avait croisée à Paris, le 1ᵉʳ juin 1905."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e38655c5-afb8-4ac5-83a1-c8f5ec80a7eb",
                        "source_entry_id": "f335b3af-ec2f-310a-a16a-fb0da884d353",
                        "target_lang_word": "ethereal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ethereal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                        "entry_id": "1b33aadf-39c1-391f-9d6f-72ee33d91453",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the presupposition of an invisible air-like element permeating all of space, or to the higher regions beyond the earth or beyond the atmosphere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccd9c845-8acd-4030-86d1-6c4fe813e9da",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: aereous, celestial"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a26cd89-77c4-4675-9ab1-e77f5f177bce",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "ethereal space"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a45451a-eff5-4fe0-8bac-32f22c7f6a77",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "ethereal regions"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a55f1923-70a9-411d-a98f-c2190ddcfe2b",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "Since to part, / Go heavenly Gueſt, Ethereal Meſſenger, / Sent from whoſe ſovran goodneſs I adore."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "724899f9-9138-4c93-98f5-747c117d5dc7",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "The fanciful fables of fairy land are but allegories of the young poet's mind when the sweet spell is upon him. Some slight thing calls up the visionary world, and all the outward and actual is for the time forgotten. It is a fever ethereal and lovely; but, like all other fevers, leaving behind weakness and exhaustion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21553bcf-10c4-4070-a099-4f67b6364fad",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "I trust that we shall be more imaginative, that our thoughts will be clearer, fresher, and more ethereal, as our sky,[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a8859c1-250c-4ea2-955f-37d9661753b0",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "She was very young—at the most nineteen, with a pale somewhat refined face, yellow hair, merry blue eyes, and shining teeth. Her beauty was of an ethereal type."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e795c640-df22-4c05-b48d-7b7c50538d88",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "Our visitors, upon the whole, were not much to boast of; and yet, sitting in a corner and very much ashamed of myself and my absurd appearance, I have again and again tasted the finest, the rarest, and the most ethereal pleasures in a glance of an eye that I should never see again—and never wanted to."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0057f10d-0bbe-4e59-a85f-a43de466c9a4",
                                                "sense_id": "e4dce698-a535-3686-b022-a296e360fc2c",
                                                "text": "Virgil described the ethereal process as expanding itself through the universe, and giving life and motion to the inhabitants of earth, water, and air, by a participation of its own essence, each particle of which returned to its native source at the dissolution of the body which it animated."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ea2e021-26c1-351b-b7d2-37c80bf5e8fe",
                                        "entry_id": "1b33aadf-39c1-391f-9d6f-72ee33d91453",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the immaterial realm, as symbolically represented by, or (in earlier epochs) conflated with, such atmospheric and extra-atmospheric concepts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e60746e0-8afe-4305-8878-74bf2f12fe90",
                                                "sense_id": "1ea2e021-26c1-351b-b7d2-37c80bf5e8fe",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: celestial, incorporeal, insubstantial, intangible, spiritual, uncorporeal, mystical, otherworldly, transcendental; see also Thesaurus:cosmic"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cc9d212-2816-4786-a34e-2eb895999285",
                                                "sense_id": "1ea2e021-26c1-351b-b7d2-37c80bf5e8fe",
                                                "text": "Sure he preſum'd of praiſe, vvho came to ſtock / Th' etherial paſtures vvith ſo fair a flock; / Burniſh'd, and bat'ning on their food, to ſhovv / The diligence of carefull herds belovv."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a4e9df3-c4e1-3533-a5c3-a475e70a60a8",
                                        "entry_id": "1b33aadf-39c1-391f-9d6f-72ee33d91453",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Consisting of ether; hence, exceedingly light or airy; tenuous; spiritlike; characterized by extreme delicacy, as form, manner, thought, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "885be0aa-8a29-4ffa-a11a-0e42b36065db",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4e9df3-c4e1-3533-a5c3-a475e70a60a8",
                                                "text": "Vaſt chain of being ! which from God began, / Ethereal Eſſence, Spirit, Subſtance, Man, / Beaſt, Bird, Fiſh, Inſect ! [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96a54e8a-fc0a-421d-92b0-154596f00c12",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4e9df3-c4e1-3533-a5c3-a475e70a60a8",
                                                "text": "Strange mystery of our nature, that those in whom genius developes itself in imagination, thus taking its most ethereal form, should yet be the most dependent on the opinions of others!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15a7e392-9080-43fd-9057-3adb00703e62",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4e9df3-c4e1-3533-a5c3-a475e70a60a8",
                                                "text": "He did not see[…]that already, in the incipiency of his work, the heavy unmalleable element of mere book-knowledge would not congenially weld with the wide fluidness and ethereal airiness of spontaneous creative thought."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "114d3a6c-f112-437b-bef8-bb015251c36f",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4e9df3-c4e1-3533-a5c3-a475e70a60a8",
                                                "text": "The innocent if lawless elf, / Ethereal in virginity, / Retains the consciousness of self."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5c97232-9aeb-4728-9636-5a0a44fc4ba4",
                                                "sense_id": "2a4e9df3-c4e1-3533-a5c3-a475e70a60a8",
                                                "text": "The hall, when emptied of its furniture, brilliantly lit, adorned with flowers whose scent tinged the air, presented a wonderful appearance of ethereal gaiety."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
